{
  "title": "Body, health and exercise",
  "note": "Describe how a body part feels with topic + adjective: 我头疼 \"I have a headache\" (literally \"I head hurts\"). 有点儿 + adjective means \"a bit\", usually for something unwelcome: 我有点儿累. 一点儿 goes after an adjective or before a noun, never before an adjective.",
  "src": { "t": "Chinese Grammar Wiki: A2 grammar points (有点儿)", "u": "https://resources.allsetlearning.com/chinese/grammar/A2_grammar_points" },
  "items": [
